m a well or spring, and an offering bowl. Tend it weekly for a month.","times":4,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Consecrate a tool","kind":"ritual","instructions":"Cleanse and consecrate one working tool. Write what you did and why.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"}]},{"title":"Correspondences, herbs and stones","intro":"What things are for: plants, stones, colours, days and planetary hours.","passed_by":"mentor","tasks":[{"title":"Twelve plants","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn twelve plants your coven works with: their uses, cautions and lore. Keep a page for each.","times":12,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Seven stones","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn seven stones and how to cleanse and charge them.","times":7,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Days and hours","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the planetary days and hours and when to use them. Plan one working by them.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"},{"title":"Herbal safety","kind":"reflection","instructions":"Write which herbs and oils need care (pregnancy, pets, skin, ingestion) and how you’ll check before using something new.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"}]},{"title":"Divination","intro":"Read for yourself and, later, for others.","passed_by":"mentor","tasks":[{"title":"Learn a system","kind":"study","instructions":"Choose a system (tarot, runes, ogham, oracle, scrying) and learn its basics.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"},{"title":"Daily draws","kind":"practice","instructions":"Draw or cast daily for thirty days and note what each meant by evening.","times":30,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Read for your mentor","kind":"practice","instructions":"Give your mentor a reading and talk through it together.","times":1,"response":"none","checked_by":"mentor"}]},{"title":"Gods, spirits and ancestors","intro":"Build relationship with the gods and spirits of the land and the ancestors, as your coven honours them.","passed_by":"mentor","tasks":[{"title":"A devotional practice","kind":"practice","instructions":"Keep a short daily devotion (an offering, a prayer, a candle) for a month.","times":30,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Honour your ancestors","kind":"ritual","instructions":"Make a place for your ancestors (of blood, of spirit or of craft) and honour them. Write about who you honoured.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"},{"title":"Discernment","kind":"reflection","instructions":"Write how you tell a real experience from wishful thinking, and when to ask for help.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"}]},{"title":"The year’s lore","intro":"Learn the four fire festivals, the old Gaelic year, and the stories of Brigid, Lugh and the Cailleach.","passed_by":"mentor","tasks":[{"title":"The lore of Imbolc · Lá Fhéile Bríde","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the history, customs and meaning of Imbolc · Lá Fhéile Bríde: The start of spring in the Gaelic year and the feast of Brigid, goddess and saint of poetry, healing and smithcraft. Brigid’s crosses are woven and a cloth is left out overnight for her blessing. Write a short page of what you found.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"self","holiday":"celtic/la_fheile_bride"},{"title":"The lore of Bealtaine","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the history, customs and meaning of Bealtaine: The start of summer. Fires were lit on the hills and cattle driven between them for protection before going out to summer pasture; in Wales it is Calan Mai. Write a short page of what you found.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"self","holiday":"celtic/bealtaine"},{"title":"The lore of Lughnasadh","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the history, customs and meaning of Lughnasadh: The harvest festival of the god Lugh, with games, hill-top gatherings, matchmaking and the first fruits of the harvest; in Wales, Gŵyl Awst. Write a short page of what you found.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"self","holiday":"celtic/lughnasadh"},{"title":"The lore of Samhain (Oíche Shamhna)","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the history, customs and meaning of Samhain (Oíche Shamhna): “Summer’s end” and the start of the Gaelic year, kept from sunset on October 31. The Otherworld draws near: fires, guising and food set out for the dead; in Wales, Calan Gaeaf. Write a short page of what you found.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"self","holiday":"celtic/samhain_gaelic"}]},{"title":"Ritual craft","intro":"Bring it all together: write and lead a ritual of your own.","passed_by":"manager","tasks":[{"title":"Write a ritual","kind":"book","instructions":"Write a complete ritual for the coven: its purpose, sacred space, the working, the words and the closing.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"manager"},{"title":"Lead it","kind":"ritual","instructions":"Lead your ritual for the coven or a few members, with your mentor present.","times":1,"response":"none","checked_by":"manager"},{"title":"Look back","kind":"reflection","instructions":"Write what went well, what you’d change, and what the training has given you.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"}]}]'::jsonb, 5)
