. Tend it weekly for a month.","times":4,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Consecrate a tool","kind":"ritual","instructions":"Cleanse and consecrate one working tool. Write what you did and why.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"}]},{"title":"Correspondences, herbs and stones","intro":"What things are for: plants, stones, colours, days and planetary hours.","passed_by":"mentor","tasks":[{"title":"Twelve plants","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn twelve plants your coven works with: their uses, cautions and lore. Keep a page for each.","times":12,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Seven stones","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn seven stones and how to cleanse and charge them.","times":7,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Days and hours","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the planetary days and hours and when to use them. Plan one working by them.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"},{"title":"Herbal safety","kind":"reflection","instructions":"Write which herbs and oils need care (pregnancy, pets, skin, ingestion) and how you’ll check before using something new.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"}]},{"title":"Divination","intro":"Read for yourself and, later, for others.","passed_by":"mentor","tasks":[{"title":"Learn a system","kind":"study","instructions":"Choose a system (tarot, runes, ogham, oracle, scrying) and learn its basics.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"},{"title":"Daily draws","kind":"practice","instructions":"Draw or cast daily for thirty days and note what each meant by evening.","times":30,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Read for your mentor","kind":"practice","instructions":"Give your mentor a reading and talk through it together.","times":1,"response":"none","checked_by":"mentor"}]},{"title":"Gods, spirits and ancestors","intro":"Build relationship with the old gods, the domovoi (house spirit) and the forefathers.","passed_by":"mentor","tasks":[{"title":"A devotional practice","kind":"practice","instructions":"Keep a short daily devotion (an offering, a prayer, a candle) for a month.","times":30,"response":"none","checked_by":"self"},{"title":"Honour your ancestors","kind":"ritual","instructions":"Make a place for your ancestors (of blood, of spirit or of craft) and honour them. Write about who you honoured.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"},{"title":"Discernment","kind":"reflection","instructions":"Write how you tell a real experience from wishful thinking, and when to ask for help.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"}]},{"title":"The year’s lore","intro":"Learn the turning year from Koliada to Kupala and Dziady, folk songs and the care of the house spirit.","passed_by":"mentor","tasks":[{"title":"The lore of Drowning of Marzanna","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the history, customs and meaning of Drowning of Marzanna: An effigy of Marzanna (Morana), the figure of winter and death, is burned or drowned to send winter away and welcome spring. Traditionally on the fourth Sunday of Lent in Poland and Czechia; many now keep it on the first day of spring or at the equinox. She is first named by the 15th-century chronicler Jan Długosz, who likened her to Ceres; whether she was ever a goddess is debated. Write a short page of what you found.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"self","holiday":"slavic/marzanna"},{"title":"The lore of Kupala Night","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the history, customs and meaning of Kupala Night: Midsummer night of fire and water: jumping over bonfires, floating flower wreaths on rivers, and searching for the magical fern flower. Kept on St John’s Eve, 23–24 June; in Orthodox lands by the Old Style, 6–7 July. Write a short page of what you found.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"self","holiday":"slavic/kupala"},{"title":"The lore of Dziady","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the history, customs and meaning of Dziady: Forefathers’ Eve, when the spirits of the ancestors are welcomed home and fed. Kept several times a year in Belarus; the autumn Dziady falls on the Saturday before St Dmitri’s day in early November, and in Poland it has merged with All Saints’ and All Souls’ (1–2 November). Write a short page of what you found.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"self","holiday":"slavic/dziady"},{"title":"The lore of Koliada","kind":"study","instructions":"Learn the history, customs and meaning of Koliada: The season of carolling: koliadki sung from house to house for blessings in the year ahead, traditionally from Christmas Eve to Epiphany (6–19 January by the Old Style). The name comes from the Latin calendae. Keeping it at the solstice as a festival of the newborn sun is a modern Rodnover (Slavic Native Faith) reconstruction; no pre-Christian Koliada is recorded. Write a short page of what you found.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"self","holiday":"slavic/koliada"}]},{"title":"Ritual craft","intro":"Bring it all together: write and lead a ritual of your own.","passed_by":"manager","tasks":[{"title":"Write a ritual","kind":"book","instructions":"Write a complete ritual for the coven: its purpose, sacred space, the working, the words and the closing.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"manager"},{"title":"Lead it","kind":"ritual","instructions":"Lead your ritual for the coven or a few members, with your mentor present.","times":1,"response":"none","checked_by":"manager"},{"title":"Look back","kind":"reflection","instructions":"Write what went well, what you’d change, and what the training has given you.","times":1,"response":"text","checked_by":"mentor"}]}]'::jsonb, 13)
